    {
      "t": "interlude",
      "text": "the clipping",
      "sub": "Elk Lodge · corkboard · undated",
      "duration": 1800
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "In Small Wood's Elk Lodge, a newspaper clipping behind glass, yellow at the edges."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Disappearances occur at a higher than normal percentile in towns such as Small Wood."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "A girl by the name of Gloria Bryant was last seen tending to chickens in a coop outside her room."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "And finally, the most very sad and true fact about a person who disappears off the face of the map is that they are most often never heard from again. There are always exceptions, as people are so prone to prove."
    },
    {
      "t": "bg",
      "src": "assets/backgrounds/vol2_scumm_tideflats_crab_vga.jpg"
    },
    {
      "t": "bgm",
      "src": "assets/audio/bgm/vol2_scumm_adlib.mp3"
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Out on the flats the crab lifts one leg and holds it there."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "It turned one eye toward the beach, an eye on a stalk as tall as the water tower."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "It was looking at me looking at it."
    },
